g terms across."},{id:"m-a-3",type:"math",difficulty:"hard",subject:"math",chapter:"Algebra",subskill:"Quadratic Equations",stem:"Solve: $x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0$",correctAnswer:"x=2, x=3",explanation:"Factor: $(x-2)(x-3) = 0$, so $x = 2$ or $x = 3$.",misconception:"Students may plug in answers instead of factoring."},{id:"m-a-4",type:"mcq",difficulty:"medium",subject:"math",chapter:"Algebra",subskill:"Polynomials",stem:"What is $(x + 3)(x - 2)$ expanded?",options:["$x^2 + x - 6$","$x^2 - x - 6$","$x^2 + 5x - 6$","$x^2 + x + 6$"],correctAnswer:0,explanation:"$x^2 - 2x + 3x - 6 = x^2 + x - 6$"},{id:"m-a-5",type:"mcq",difficulty:"easy",subject:"math",chapter:"Algebra",subskill:"Linear Equations",stem:"Which equation has slope 2 and y-intercept 3?",options:["$y = 2x + 3$","$y = 3x + 2$","$y = 2x - 3$","$y = 3x - 2$"],correctAnswer:0,explanation:"Slope-intercept form is $y = mx + b$ where $m=2, b=3$."}],Geometry:[{id:"m-g-1",type:"mcq",difficulty:"easy",subject:"math",chapter:"Geometry",subskill:"Triangles",stem:"What is the sum of angles in a triangle?",options:["90\xb0","180\xb0","270\xb0","360\xb0"],correctAnswer:1,explanation:"The sum of interior angles in any triangle is 180\xb0.",misconception:"Some students think it's 90\xb0 confusing it with a right angle."},{id:"m-g-2",type:"math",difficulty:"medium",subject:"math",chapter:"Geometry",subskill:"Area",stem:"Find the area of a circle with radius $r = 7$ cm (use $pi approx \frac{22}{7}$).",correctAnswer:"154",explanation:"Area = $pi r^2 = \frac{22}{7} 	imes 49 = 154$ cm\xb2",misconception:"Using diameter instead of radius in formula."},{id:"m-g-3",type:"mcq",difficulty:"hard",subject:"math",chapter:"Geometry",subskill:"Similarity",stem:"Two triangles are similar. Sides of first are 3, 4, 5. Corresponding side of second is 6. What is its perimeter?",options:["12","18","24","30"],correctAnswer:1,explanation:"Scale factor is $6/3 = 2$. Perimeter of first = 12. Second = $12 	imes 2 = 24$. Wait — 3+4+5=12, scaled = 24."},{id:"m-g-4",type:"mcq",difficulty:"easy",subject:"math",chapter:"Geometry",subskill:"Triangles",stem:"In a right triangle, if two angles are 30\xb0 and 60\xb0, what is the third angle?",options:["30\xb0","60\xb0","90\xb0","45\xb0"],correctAnswer:2,explanation:"Sum of angles = 180\xb0, so $180 - 30 - 60 = 90\xb0$. Also definition of right triangle."},{id:"m-g-5",type:"mcq",difficulty:"medium",subject:"math",chapter:"Geometry",subskill:"Circles",stem:"The diameter of a circle is 14 cm. What is its circumference?",options:["22 cm","44 cm","14 cm","28 cm"],correctAnswer:1,explanation:"Circumference = $pi d = \frac{22}{7} 	imes 14 = 44$ cm"}],Trigonometry:[{id:"m-t-1",type:"mcq",difficulty:"easy",subject:"math",chapter:"Trigonometry",subskill:"Ratios",stem:"What is $sin(30\xb0)$?",options:["$\frac{1}{2}$","$\frac{sqrt{3}}{2}$","$\frac{sqrt{2}}{2}$","1"],correctAnswer:0,explanation:"$sin(30\xb0) = \frac{1}{2}$ is a fundamental trigonometric value."},{id:"m-t-2",type:"mcq",difficulty:"medium",subject:"math",chapter:"Trigonometry",subskill:"Identities",stem:"What is $sin^2	heta + cos^2	heta$?",options:["0","1","2","$	an	heta$"],correctAnswer:1,explanation:"This is the Pythagorean identity: $sin^2	heta + cos^2	heta = 1$."},{id:"m-t-3",type:"math",difficulty:"hard",subject:"math",chapter:"Trigonometry",subskill:"Applications",stem:"A ladder 10 m long leans against a wall at 60\xb0. Find the height it reaches. (Use $sin 60\xb0 = \frac{sqrt{3}}{2}$)",correctAnswer:"$5sqrt{3}$",explanation:"Height = $10 	imes sin(60\xb0) = 10 	imes \frac{sqrt{3}}{2} = 5sqrt{3}$ m",misconception:"Confusing sine and cosine when choosing the ratio."}],Calculus:[{id:"m-c-1",type:"mcq",difficulty:"medium",subject:"math",chapter:"Calculus",subskill:"Derivatives",stem:"What is the derivative of $x^3$?",options:["$3x^2$","$x^2$","$3x$","$3x^3$"],correctAnswer:0,explanation:"Using the power rule: $\frac{d}{dx}(x^n) = nx^{n-1}$, so $3x^2$."},{id:"m-c-2",type:"math",difficulty:"hard",subject:"math",chapter:"Calculus",subskill:"Integration",stem:"Evaluate: $int x^2 , dx$",correctAnswer:"$\frac{x^3}{3} + C$",explanation:"Using power rule for integration: $int x^n dx = \frac{x^{n+1}}{n+1} + C$"}]},science:{Physics:[{id:"s-p-1",type:"mcq",difficulty:"easy",subject:"science",chapter:"Physics",subskill:"Motion",stem:"What is the SI unit of velocity?",options:["m/s","m/s\xb2","km/h","m"],correctAnswer:0,explanation:"Velocity = displacement/time, so SI unit is m/s."},{id:"s-p-2",type:"mcq",difficulty:"medium",subject:"science",chapter:"Physics",subskill:"Force",stem:"Newton's second law: $F = ma$. If mass is doubled and force constant, acceleration becomes?",options:["Same","Double","Half","Quadruple"],correctAnswer:2,explanation:"$a = F/m$, so if $m$ doubles, $a$ becomes half.",misconception:"Students often think more mass means more acceleration."},{id:"s-p-3",type:"mcq",difficulty:"easy",subject:"science",chapter:"Physics",subskill:"Energy",stem:"What type of energy does a stretched rubber band have?",options:["Kinetic","Potential","Thermal","Sound"],correctAnswer:1,explanation:"A stretched rubber band stores elastic potential energy."}],Chemistry:[{id:"s-c-1",type:"mcq",difficulty:"easy",subject:"science",chapter:"Chemistry",subskill:"Atomic Structure",stem:"What is the atomic number of Carbon?",options:["4","6","12","14"],correctAnswer:1,explanation:"Carbon has 6 protons, so atomic number = 6."},{id:"s-c-2",type:"mcq",difficulty:"medium",subject:"science",chapter:"Chemistry",subskill:"Chemical Reactions",stem:"What type of reaction is $A + B \rightarrow AB$?",options:["Decomposition","Combination","Displacement","Double displacement"],correctAnswer:1,explanation:"Two reactants combining to form one product is a combination reaction."},{id:"s-c-3",type:"math",difficulty:"hard",subject:"science",chapter:"Chemistry",subskill:"Stoichiometry",stem:"In the reaction $2H_2 + O_2 \rightarrow 2H_2O$, how many moles of water are produced from 3 moles of $H_2$?",correctAnswer:"3",explanation:"From stoichiometry: 2 moles H₂ → 2 moles H₂O, so 3 moles H₂ → 3 moles H₂O."}],Biology:[{id:"s-b-1",type:"mcq",difficulty:"easy",subject:"science",chapter:"Biology",subskill:"Cells",stem:"What is the powerhouse of the cell?",options:["Nucleus","Mitochondria","Ribosome","Chloroplast"],correctAnswer:1,explanation:"Mitochondria produce ATP through cellular respiration."},{id:"s-b-2",type:"mcq",difficulty:"medium",subject:"science",chapter:"Biology",subskill:"Photosynthesis",stem:"Which gas is released during photosynthesis?",options:["CO₂","O₂","N₂","H₂"],correctAnswer:1,explanation:"Plants release oxygen as a byproduct of photosynthesis."},{id:"s-b-3",type:"mcq",difficulty:"hard",subject:"science",chapter:"Biology",subskill:"Genetics",stem:"What is the probability of getting a homozygous dominant offspring from two heterozygous parents?",options:["0%","25%","50%","75%"],correctAnswer:1,explanation:"Punnett square shows 1/4 (25%) chance of homozygous dominant."}]},english:{Grammar:[{id:"e-g-1",type:"mcq",difficulty:"easy",subject:"english",chapter:"Grammar",subskill:"Tenses",stem:"She ___ to school every day.",options:["go","goes","going","gone"],correctAnswer:1,explanation:"Third person singular in present simple adds -s: 'goes'."},{id:"e-g-2",type:"mcq",difficulty:"medium",subject:"english",chapter:"Grammar",subskill:"Parts of Speech",stem:'Identify the adjective: "The quick brown fox jumps."',options:["quick","fox","jumps","the"],correctAnswer:0,explanation:"Adjectives describe nouns. 'Quick' describes the fox."},{id:"e-g-3",type:"mcq",difficulty:"hard",subject:"english",chapter:"Grammar",subskill:"Conditionals",stem:"If I ___ rich, I would travel the world. (Second conditional)",options:["am","was","were","be"],correctAnswer:2,explanation:"Second conditional uses 'were' for all subjects (subjunctive)."}],Comprehension:[{id:"e-co-1",type:"mcq",difficulty:"easy",subject:"english",chapter:"Comprehension",subskill:"Reading",stem:"What is the main idea of a paragraph?",options:["The last sentence","The central thought","A supporting detail","A question"],correctAnswer:1,explanation:"The main idea is the central thought the paragraph conveys."},{id:"e-co-2",type:"mcq",difficulty:"medium",subject:"english",chapter:"Comprehension",subskill:"Inference",stem:"If a character is described as having 'a forced smile', what can you infer?",options:["They are happy","They are hiding feelings","They are angry","They are tired"],correctAnswer:1,explanation:"A 'forced' smile suggests the emotion isn't genuine."}],Writing:[{id:"e-w-1",type:"mcq",difficulty:"medium",subject:"english",chapter:"Writing",subskill:"Essay",stem:"Which sentence best introduces an essay topic?",options:["The topic sentence","The conclusion","A random fact","A question"],correctAnswer:0,explanation:"A topic sentence clearly introduces the main idea of a paragraph."}]}},q={math:[{day:1,title:"Linear Equations",description:"Master solving one-variable linear equations.",activity:"5 practice problems + video lesson",duration:"20 min",completed:!1},{day:2,title:"Geometry Basics",description:"Learn area and perimeter formulas.",activity:"Interactive geometry worksheet",duration:"25 min",completed:!1},{day:3,title:"Trigonometry Ratios",description:"Memorize and apply sin, cos, tan values.",activity:"Flashcards + 10 practice questions",duration:"20 min",completed:!1},{day:4,title:"Quadratic Equations",description:"Learn factoring and the quadratic formula.",activity:"Step-by-step tutorial + quiz",duration:"30 min",completed:!1},{day:5,title:"Practice Test",description:"Mixed practice on all topics.",activity:"20-question timed test",duration:"30 min",completed:!1}],science:[{day:1,title:"Motion & Force",description:"Understand velocity, acceleration, and Newton's laws.",activity:"Simulation experiment + worksheet",duration:"25 min",completed:!1},{day:2,title:"Atomic Structure",description:"Electrons, protons, neutrons and Bohr model.",activity:"Interactive periodic table 